WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.443 --> 00:00:04.058
Let's just think about addiction,

00:00:04.442 --> 00:00:08.267
because in biology
and in psychology, frankly,

00:00:08.589 --> 00:00:12.113
it really often pays
to think about the extremes first

00:00:12.114 --> 00:00:14.960
and then work our way
towards more typical circumstances.

00:00:14.961 --> 00:00:15.943
Now with that said,

00:00:15.944 --> 00:00:18.325
addiction unfortunately,
is very common nowadays.

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:24.624
I just heard a statistic, in fact,
that there is an 80% increase

00:00:24.625 --> 00:00:28.286
in alcohol use disorder
among women in the last 30 years.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:29.499
I talked a little bit about this

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.329
in the episode that I did
about alcohol and health.

00:00:32.843 --> 00:00:33.816
Again, I want to be very clear.

00:00:33.817 --> 00:00:36.971
I'm not somebody that is completely
against alcohol for adults,

00:00:36.972 --> 00:00:38.657
provided they're not alcoholics.

00:00:39.083 --> 00:00:42.200
Turns out two drinks a week,
probably fine health-wise.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.071
Zero would be better if we're honest.

00:00:45.072 --> 00:00:47.080
Zero is better than any alcohol.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.082
But two drinks a week is probably fine.

00:00:49.083 --> 00:00:50.972
Past two drinks,
you start running into problems.

00:00:51.408 --> 00:00:55.067
Yet many, many people out there,
male and female alike

00:00:55.914 --> 00:01:00.157
suffer from alcohol use disorder,
also called alcoholism.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:03.829
The same is also true
for things like methamphetamine

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:07.457
or cocaine
or other types of substance addictions.

00:01:08.914 --> 00:01:11.116
The same is also true
for a lot of behavioral

00:01:11.117 --> 00:01:13.320
or what are sometimes
called process addictions.

00:01:13.321 --> 00:01:16.133
Things like sex addiction
or video game addiction,

00:01:16.257 --> 00:01:22.457
or any type of behavior that, frankly,
is leveraging the dopamine system,

00:01:22.557 --> 00:01:25.749
but that engages
this progressive narrowing

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:30.119
of the things that bring someone pleasure
such that nothing else is really salient.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.343
Nothing else is really pulling them in

00:01:32.344 --> 00:01:37.486
in the way that their video games
or sex or pornography or alcohol.

00:01:38.157 --> 00:01:42.257
Pick your substance
or behavior that you see out there,

00:01:42.258 --> 00:01:43.742
or hopefully not,

00:01:43.986 --> 00:01:46.040
that you might suffer
from an addiction to.

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:47.760
What's happening in addiction?

00:01:48.129 --> 00:01:51.666
Well, addiction involves dopamine,
among other things,

00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:54.109
often the opioid system, etc.

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:58.443
But if we were to think
about what's the stimulus in an addiction

00:01:58.444 --> 00:02:00.900
and what's the peak in dopamine,

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:04.140
and then what happens after that peak,

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:07.882
it all becomes very clear
as to why addiction happens

00:02:07.883 --> 00:02:09.686
and why it's so pernicious.

00:02:10.116 --> 00:02:12.007
For instance, let's take cocaine.

00:02:12.008 --> 00:02:17.006
Cocaine causes dramatic increases
in dopamine very, very fast.

00:02:17.314 --> 00:02:21.240
If somebody craves cocaine,
what are they craving?

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:22.686
They're craving that dopamine peak.

00:02:22.687 --> 00:02:26.057
They're craving
the increased level of alertness.

00:02:26.142 --> 00:02:30.657
They're craving a number of things
associated with the feeling of being

00:02:30.658 --> 00:02:32.300
under the influence of the drug.

00:02:32.542 --> 00:02:36.479
But the stimulus for it simply
becomes that line of cocaine.

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:37.680
Or in the case of crack,

00:02:37.681 --> 00:02:39.800
that crack rock
that they're going to smoke

00:02:40.325 --> 00:02:43.458
and God forbid they're mainlining it,
they're shooting into a vein.

00:02:43.889 --> 00:02:49.013
What happens is they snort,
smoke, or inject cocaine

00:02:49.014 --> 00:02:55.071
and dopamine levels almost immediately
go up to a very high peak.

00:02:55.243 --> 00:03:00.529
The time gap between the stimulus
and the dopamine is very, very short.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:05.900
So short, in fact, that there's really
no other contingencies in between

00:03:06.029 --> 00:03:09.186
that the mesocortical system
has to learn.

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:12.440
In fact, what does the system "learn"?

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:17.400
It learns cocaine equals
massive amounts of dopamine

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:20.960
equals feeling
euphoric and energetic, etc.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:25.386
In doing that,
it reinforces the whole circuit

00:03:25.443 --> 00:03:27.429
so that that short,

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:32.520
we can even say hyper-short contingency
is really what the system wants.

00:03:33.108 --> 00:03:37.232
So much so
that longer contingencies of, say,

00:03:37.233 --> 00:03:41.542
putting in the hard work
of generating a fitness program

00:03:41.543 --> 00:03:43.566
or a professional program for yourself

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:47.732
or an education program
which takes not just many days

00:03:47.733 --> 00:03:48.966
but many weeks and years,

00:03:48.967 --> 00:03:51.749
well, none of that is going
to lead to peaks in dopamine

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:55.571
that are as high as the peak
in dopamine associated with cocaine.

00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:57.725
That tells us something critical.

00:03:58.275 --> 00:04:03.574
It is both the duration
between desire and effect.

00:04:03.575 --> 00:04:04.307
When I say effect,

00:04:04.308 --> 00:04:07.308
I mean the rewarding properties
of dopamine that are experienced.

00:04:07.309 --> 00:04:08.149
That's important.

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:13.680
Very short gaps teach the system
to expect and want short gaps.

00:04:14.286 --> 00:04:17.129
Makes it very hard
to pursue things that take longer.

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:23.143
When we say it's the short,
or in this case, hyper-short distance

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:26.080
or time
between the stimulus and the dopamine,

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:27.417
what we're really talking about,

00:04:27.418 --> 00:04:30.671
if we were to plot this out
on a board or on a piece of paper,

00:04:30.729 --> 00:04:33.416
is the steepness of the rise of that peak.

00:04:33.417 --> 00:04:34.799
It's very, very steep.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:38.714
The peak in dopamine
is coming up very fast after the desire.

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:43.520
In addition to that,
and this is very important,

00:04:43.918 --> 00:04:48.467
the higher the peak in dopamine
and the faster the rise to that peak,

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:54.350
the further below baseline the dopamine
drops after the drug wears off.

00:04:54.813 --> 00:04:56.066
In the case of cocaine,

00:04:56.067 --> 00:04:59.357
it's a very fast
and very large rise in dopamine,

00:04:59.625 --> 00:05:02.325
followed by a steep drop

00:05:02.983 --> 00:05:06.650
and very deep trough
in dopamine below baseline.

00:05:07.492 --> 00:05:10.975
You say, okay, so there's pleasure,
then there's lack of pleasure.

00:05:11.883 --> 00:05:15.617
But it's worse than that
because it's not just lack of pleasure.

00:05:15.925 --> 00:05:18.160
If you recall
what we talked about a little bit earlier,

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:24.092
that drop below baseline triggers
the desire and the pursuit for what?

00:05:24.383 --> 00:05:25.425
For more.

00:05:25.914 --> 00:05:28.207
This sets in motion a vicious loop

00:05:28.208 --> 00:05:30.882
where people start
pursuing peaks in dopamine

00:05:30.883 --> 00:05:33.033
that can come
very fast without much effort.

00:05:33.958 --> 00:05:37.342
That's one of the ways
in which addiction start to take hold.

00:05:38.733 --> 00:05:40.332
There's a simple way to think about this

00:05:40.333 --> 00:05:43.216
and to remember if you want
to avoid this whole thing.

00:05:43.217 --> 00:05:45.416
I mean, the first one is obvious,
don't do cocaine.

00:05:45.417 --> 00:05:46.491
Don't try it. Don't use it.

00:05:46.492 --> 00:05:48.225
Certainly don't get addicted to it.

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:50.317
Those are all one in the same, frankly.

00:05:50.318 --> 00:05:55.016
I don't know many people
that despite opinions to the contrary

00:05:55.017 --> 00:05:59.024
that use cocaine recreationally,
that don't at some point run into either

00:05:59.025 --> 00:06:03.399
a financial, psychological,
physical, or some other problem.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:05.629
The other thing that's absolutely
critical to keep in mind,

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:09.342
and this was discussed
in my colleague Dr. Anna Lembke's book,

00:06:09.343 --> 00:06:11.559
Dopamine Nation and on this podcast.

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:12.457
Excellent book, by the way.

00:06:12.458 --> 00:06:14.515
I highly recommend it
if you haven't read it already.

00:06:14.516 --> 00:06:18.991
It's a fascinating exploration
into dopamine as it relates to addiction,

00:06:18.992 --> 00:06:21.443
not just drug addiction,
but other types of addiction.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:23.282
Again, the name of that book
is Dopamine Nation.

00:06:23.283 --> 00:06:25.383
We'll provide a link to it
in the show notes captions.

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:28.383
The other thing that happens

00:06:28.384 --> 00:06:33.408
after those big, fast increases
in dopamine caused by things like cocaine

00:06:33.792 --> 00:06:38.092
is afterwards
when it quickly drops below baseline,

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:43.658
it takes a much longer time
to get back to the original baseline

00:06:43.908 --> 00:06:46.033
than it did prior to using the drug.

00:06:46.767 --> 00:06:51.796
Worse still, is that the peaks
in dopamine that are created

00:06:52.008 --> 00:06:57.558
from more consumption of cocaine
leads to progressively lower peaks

00:06:58.371 --> 00:07:01.129
and deeper troughs below baseline.

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:03.741
The whole system
is shifting away from pleasure

00:07:03.742 --> 00:07:07.825
and more to pain
and the desire for pursuit of the drug.

